,"custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T19:05:22-07:00","id":1382656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382527-reminder-about-vampire-novels?p=1382647#post1382647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anybody know how much it costs to have an audiobook made? Assuming it's not mind blowingly expensive, I'm willing to bet WW/Onyx Path could easily get the crowdfunding done to make audiobooks out of the clan novels, tribe novels, ascension war trilogy, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crossroad Press offered to do the audiobooks. They were turned down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T19:14:08-07:00","id":1382658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382527-reminder-about-vampire-novels?p=1382656#post1382656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossroad Press offered to do the audiobooks. They were turned down.</div> </div> </div> </div> That sucks. Is there a reason? Audiobooks are great, and it would be a great way to re-monetize a bunch of assets they're otherwise just sitting on. People who may already own all the books, and have read them, may still pony up for the audiobooks just to experience them a new way.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T19:17:40-07:00","id":1382660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382527-reminder-about-vampire-novels?p=1382658#post1382658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That sucks. Is there a reason? Audiobooks are great, and it would be a great way to re-monetize a bunch of assets they're otherwise just sitting on. People who may already own all the books, and have read them, may still pony up for the audiobooks just to experience them a new way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, I don't know. I think they should have re-released all their old catalog in multiple formats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T08:58:49-07:00","id":1382767,"title":"","content":"The Nosferatu investigates on the murder of their Justicar Petrodon. They suspect on Giovanni involvement and kidnap Benito Giovanni (influential Giovanni from Boston), then find about someone named Nickolai (Tremere antitribu), a contact from him. The Nosferatu also understand that Anatole is &quot;the Harbinger of Gehenna&quot; and have someone follow and report his every movement. Khalil Ravana is tricked by a girl into servitude to Hazimel.<br /> <br /> ur-Shulgi awakens from almost two millennia being in torpor, kills the Caliph, then kills Jamal and becomes the Old Man of the Mountain.<br /> <br /> The main intention of Moncada gathering this war party was to triumph then leave Spain and go to Mexico and become Regent. Polonia, Vykos and Borges are the main generals of the attack. Vykos hire Lucita to kill Borges, the Archbishop of Miami. Moncada knows this and hires Talley to protect Borges (expecting him to fail against her daughter). Parmenides is hired by the Sabbat and his function, beyond being Vykos toy, is to enter chantries and kill Tremere.<br /> <br /> The east coast war starts in Atlanta killing most of the residents (further info on the characters is in Necropolis Atlanta). Victoria Ash is captured by Tzimisce and is permanently marked by Vykos. Vykos is being fed information on Camarilla defenses from &quot;Lucius&quot;. The Setite Vegel looks for the eye under Hesha's orders, he puts it on but dies. The eye is now on Leopold, a &quot;Toreador&quot; who believes that Victoria Ash is his sire, goes to NYC. Vykos attack DC, kills Vitel's childe Monica Black, throws her head to him and then Vitel escapes.<br /> <br /> Prince Benedict of Atlanta survives through weird reality tampering against the Sabbat but he is diablerized by Anatole afterwards. Victoria Ash is rescued and along with the General (an elder Malkavian with Protean at 5 at least) they defeat both Sebastian (Borges childe) and her Tzimisce captor, Elford.<br /> <br /> Hesha embraces Elizabeth Dimitros who has weird dreams and through them she explains the events of the Week of Nightmares. Khalil Ravana then kind of take Elizabeth away from Hesha.<br /> <br /> Pieterzoon, Vitel, Bell, Xaviar and Alexander Garlotte (Prince of Baltimore) becomes the Camarilla resistence of the east coast Sabbat attack. Garlotte is killed by one of his childer and Theo Bell let such childe go without ever telling anyone. Leopold in now in Adirondack Park (northwest of NYC IIRC), quite insane and leaving a trail of dead bodies. There is a Gangrel gather with Pilar Salvador Ramona, her sire and some more, one being a shaman (Blackfeather IIRC) who gives Ramona a &quot;sight&quot; on the eye/leopold thing. They attack him, things goes BAD, [Tzimisce]'s influence on NYC + Chimerstry 9 of the eye of Hazimel makes Leopold go full power against all the Gangrel. Only Ramona and Xaviar survive.<br /> <br /> Anatole goes to the cave writes a scrawl that nobody understands with his ripped off arm and perishes, this is reported to Calebros. (he never put the eye on himself)<br /> <br /> Lucita knows that Moncada summons her approximately once a century, he does now. Due to his bond to her, Lucita and Fatima bond each other to have an advantage when they face him. Leviathan (his abyssal guardian) target those who aren't of Moncada's blood, and all having Moncada's blood atm, messed up his directives and attacked Moncada, this let Fatima have the kill blow against the Archbishop.<br /> <br /> Isabel is tasked to babysit Chas Tello Giovanni and search for Benito Giovanni. They end up finding a ridiculously old Cappadocian in New Orleans who kill Chas and let Isabel live (in favor to Ambrogino IIRC).<br /> <br /> Theo finds that Lucius is Vitel and traps and kill him (but definitely not expecting him surviving to a dragonsbreath shot to the head, using Thaumaturgy and Obtenebration and killing most of those who fought alonside him). &quot;Toughest 'Ventrue' ever!&quot; - Theo to Pieterzoon<br /> <br /> With Moncada and Borges dead, Vykos being archbishop of DC, the crusade falls to Polonia but the learns of affairs in NYC that the Camarilla is getting the city back, ending the crusade.<br /> <br /> Only Leopold remains, now without the massive Vicissitude/Koldunic power. Ramona uses bloodroot to neutralize the connection of Leopold and the eye, and Bell defeats him. Victoria embraces him before his death as she too believe that he was her childe.<br /> <br /> Anatole's scrawl is deciphered and mentions that the one who killed Petrodon is still around, which is Nickolai, who is the real sire of Leopold (true name being Gary Pennington). Cock Robin finds Nickolai in the sewers attempting to escape and avenge his sire.<br /> <br /> - Saga<br /> <br /> PS: the one thing that happened during the crusade and was left out of the novels was the death of Boukephos during the attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 04-20-2020, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T00:18:44-07:00","id":1383107,"title":"","content":"Thanks Saga, this was really helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T14:37:32-07:00","id":1383227,"title":"","content":"Were these books just the novelization of White Wolf employees' own home campaign(s)? Because that's really the impression I get whenever I hear the plots described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T12:23:18-07:00","id":1383420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bb